                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b2883fc9-f098-3f66-94a8-494d4eeaa656",
                        "entry_id": "4a26a779-97fc-37c9-a9b9-b2ec8d70c9a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "лингв. расположение одного из связанных между собой элементов (слова или члена предложения) перед другим"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d477db77-85c9-4039-bdb9-4b039afb0481",
                                "sense_id": "b2883fc9-f098-3f66-94a8-494d4eeaa656",
                                "text": "Как русские, так и украинские писатели используют препозицию прямого дополнения не только как средство стилизации разговорной речи и для передачи тончайших оттенков мысли."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "21e83d5b-b940-4e34-bab6-dc92a5bfc3f1",
                        "source_entry_id": "4a26a779-97fc-37c9-a9b9-b2ec8d70c9a2",
                        "source_sense_id": "b2883fc9-f098-3f66-94a8-494d4eeaa656",
                        "target_lang_word": "preposition",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "preposition",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ff13730-9aa1-351a-99a7-33bf2c311cc1",
                                        "entry_id": "3d7eeb70-4c67-38fd-8c4b-9e53c7dbafcc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of a class of non-inflecting words and multiword terms typically employed to connect a following noun or a pronoun, in an adjectival or adverbial sense, with some other word: a particle used with a noun or pronoun (in English always in the objective case) to make a phrase limiting some other word."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "strict-sense"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64093cbd-77da-4332-9a05-7d3419ced491",
                                                "sense_id": "2ff13730-9aa1-351a-99a7-33bf2c311cc1",
                                                "text": "322. The parts of speech which are neither declined nor conjugated, are called by the general name of particles. 323. They are adverbs, prepositions, conjunctions, and interjections."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c58fd619-22b4-4f82-9dfd-54c5d650fcc8",
                                                "sense_id": "2ff13730-9aa1-351a-99a7-33bf2c311cc1",
                                                "text": "And in (121) below, we see that when a wh-NP is used as the Object of a Preposition, the whole Prepositional Phrase can undergo WH MOVEMENT:\n (121) (a) [To whom] can I send this letter —?\n (121) (b) [About what] are they quarrelling —?\n (121) (c) [In which book] did you read about it —?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48774d41-caa5-48ea-93d3-cf0681ada66c",
                                                "sense_id": "2ff13730-9aa1-351a-99a7-33bf2c311cc1",
                                                "text": "I love this girl. “On which I can get my hands” — even in her darkest moment, she cannot bring herself to end a sentence with a preposition."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d0dc6e5-268f-3a0b-a36b-851b5dc6c59f",
                                        "entry_id": "3d7eeb70-4c67-38fd-8c4b-9e53c7dbafcc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An adposition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04e88a06-921d-3110-b408-8f8c804f48df",
                                        "entry_id": "3d7eeb70-4c67-38fd-8c4b-9e53c7dbafcc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A proposition; an exposition; a discourse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5aef31bd-2b87-42d8-b716-d2c5769ddb11",
                                                "sense_id": "04e88a06-921d-3110-b408-8f8c804f48df",
                                                "text": "[…] he made a longe preposicion & oracion cōcernynge yͤ allegiaūce which he exortyd his lordes to owe"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
